# ==============================================================================
# PROJECT ENVIRONMENT SAMPLE (the socle)
# ==============================================================================
# What THIS project needs. The gmake Makefile loads the shared .env.global
# first, then this file — every value set here wins for this project only.
#
# Build your copy and fill it in:
#   gmake env_project_enable
#
# That command reads this sample and those of every installed pack, and writes
# ./.env — adding the variables that are missing, never rewriting one that is
# already there.
#
# RULE: anything that identifies THIS project lives here, never in
# .env.global — project ids, resource names, service names.
# ==============================================================================

# The packs add the variables they need below this line: each block sits next
# to the modules that read it, and `gmake env_project_enable` copies it in.
